{#
  ABOUT THIS SITE. Footer link only, never the main nav: it is a colophon, and
  a colophon that competes with Contact for attention has misunderstood itself.

  THREE PARTS, ONE PAGE, IN ORDER. An essay saying what the site is for, a
  colophon saying what it is made of, and a scoreboard saying what that costs.
  Each one earns the next: the claim, the method, the evidence.

  ============================================================
  EVERY NUMBER ON THIS PAGE IS DERIVED OR MEASURED. NONE IS TYPED.
  ============================================================

  Two sources and the page labels which is which on every row.

  DERIVED, live, at build time: the article counts, straight off the
  collections. These cannot go stale, because they are recomputed on every
  build from the same data that builds the articles themselves.

  MEASURED, dated, from src/_data/siteStats.json: everything that needs a
  browser or a stopwatch. Bytes, requests, timings. Written by
  `npm run measure:stats`, which builds the site, serves it, loads every page in
  headless Chromium and records what actually arrived. Re-run it and the numbers
  move; that is the point.

  THE EMBARRASSING ONES ARE ON HERE TOO, which is the only reason the rest are
  worth reading. Three third-party requests on the median page and not one page
  at zero, because Lora is served by Google Fonts. A worst-case CLS above zero
  on every page. A median page weight north of 300 KB, most of it the six
  self-hosted weights of the display face. A reader with devtools open will find
  all three in about a minute, and a scoreboard that had quietly omitted them
  would be worth nothing.

  NO NEW TOKENS. The layout has more personality than the marketing pages,
  which the brief allows, but every value in about-this-site.css resolves to a
  token that already exists.
#}

{% call container(class="cs-about") %}

  {#- ---- 1. THE ESSAY ---- -#}
  <header class="cs-about__head">
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">Colophon</p>
    <h1 class="cs-about__title">About this site</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="cs-about__essay">
    <p>
      We used to run this site the way we run a client's. A service page for
      every service, titles built to be found, the words arranged so a search
      engine would know exactly which aisle we were standing in. That is real
      work and we still do it, because plenty of clients need to be found and
      being found is the job.
    </p>
    <p>
      We have been lucky enough to stay busy through clients and friends who
      send people our way. Which means this site does not have to go out and get
      the work. It only has to be true.
    </p>
    <p>
      So it turned into the place we get to build properly. Tooling we wanted an
      excuse to try, design decisions argued down to the last pixel, and a way of
      writing the work up that sounds like people talking rather than a brochure.
      We closed the social accounts. We have never advertised. Nobody here has to
      write "Welcome to our Laguna Beach SEO Agency in Laguna Beach" ever again.
    </p>
    <p>
      One honest exception. The Yelp material is not marketing for the work. It
      is the work, written down, with the parts we are still unsure about marked
      as unsure.
    </p>
  </div>

  {#- ---- 2. THE COLOPHON. Facts, no adjectives. ---- -#}
  <section class="cs-about__section">
    <h2 class="cs-about__h2">Built with</h2>

    <dl class="cs-about__colophon">
      <div>
        <dt>Eleventy</dt>
        <dd>Static site generator. Every page is HTML on disk before a reader asks for it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Vite</dt>
        <dd>Asset pipeline. Hashes and bundles the one stylesheet and the one script.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Tailwind</dt>
        <dd>Utility layer under hand-written component CSS, not instead of it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Cloudflare Pages</dt>
        <dd>Hosting. A push to the main branch is the deploy.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Git</dt>
        <dd>The source of truth. Every word and every rule on this site has a commit behind it.</dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Dual and Lora</dt>
        <dd>
          Display and body. Dual is self-hosted from this origin. Lora is served
          by Google Fonts, which is the third-party request counted below.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <ul class="cs-about__not">
      <li>No CMS</li>
      <li>No database</li>
      <li>No plugins</li>
      <li>No cookies</li>
      <li>No tracking pixels</li>
      <li>No third-party scripts</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="cs-about__note">
      Structured data on every page, matching what is visible on it. Sources
      dated on every article. Pages corrected when the facts move, rather than
      left standing because they already ranked.
    </p>
  </section>

  {#- ---- 3. THE SCOREBOARD ---- -#}
  <section class="cs-about__section">
    <h2 class="cs-about__h2">Measured</h2>
    <p class="cs-about__note">
      Nothing below is typed by hand. Rows marked <span class="cs-about__src">derived</span>
      are recomputed on every build. Rows marked
      <span class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</span> come from
      <code>npm run measure:stats</code>, which builds the site, serves it, and
      loads every page in headless Chromium. {{ siteStats.how }}
    </p>

    <div class="cs-about__stats">

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.build.pagesWritten }}</p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">Pages built</p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

      {#- DERIVED LIVE, one per tier and never summed. Adding them would make
          one number out of two different things: the Yelp Hub tier is published
          writing, and the library tier today is the two build fixtures
          ARTICLE_SYSTEM.md has marked for deletion. A total would hide that. -#}
      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ collections.yelpArticles | length }}</p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">Articles, Yelp Hub tier</p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">derived</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ collections.library | length }}</p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">Articles, library tier</p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">derived</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.build.ms }}<span class="cs-about__unit">ms</span></p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">Full build, cold</p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.js.bytes }}<span class="cs-about__unit">bytes</span></p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">
          JavaScript shipped, every page. {{ siteStats.js.gzipBytes }} bytes gzipped.
        </p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.weight.medianGzipKb }}<span class="cs-about__unit">KB</span></p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">
          Median page, gzipped as production serves it. {{ siteStats.weight.medianKb }} KB uncompressed.
        </p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.weight.medianRequests }}</p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">Requests to this origin, median page</p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

      {#- THE ONE WE WOULD RATHER NOT PRINT. It goes on because the page is only
          worth reading if the numbers are checkable, and this one is checkable
          in about a minute with a network panel open. -#}
      <div class="cs-about__stat cs-about__stat--flag">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.thirdParty.medianRequestsPerPage }}</p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">
          Third-party requests, median page. {{ siteStats.thirdParty.maxRequestsOnAPage }} at
          the worst, and {{ siteStats.thirdParty.pagesWithNone }} pages at zero. Every host
          contacted anywhere on the site: {% for host in siteStats.thirdParty.hosts %}{{ host.host }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
        </p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.vitals.lcpMedianMs }}<span class="cs-about__unit">ms</span></p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">
          Largest contentful paint, median page. {{ siteStats.vitals.lcpWorstMs }} ms at the worst.
        </p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}, lab</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat cs-about__stat--flag">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.vitals.clsWorst }}</p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">
          Worst cumulative layout shift of any page. {{ siteStats.vitals.pagesAtZeroCls }} pages at zero.
        </p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}, lab</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.weight.heaviest.gzipKb }}<span class="cs-about__unit">KB</span></p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">
          Heaviest page, gzipped: <a href="{{ siteStats.weight.heaviest.url }}">{{ siteStats.weight.heaviest.url }}</a>
        </p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-about__stat">
        <p class="cs-about__figure">{{ siteStats.weight.lightest.gzipKb }}<span class="cs-about__unit">KB</span></p>
        <p class="cs-about__label">
          Lightest page, gzipped: <a href="{{ siteStats.weight.lightest.url }}">{{ siteStats.weight.lightest.url }}</a>
        </p>
        <p class="cs-about__src">measured {{ siteStats.measuredAt }}</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p class="cs-about__note cs-about__note--last">
      {{ siteStats.vitals.note }} The page weight is dominated by six self-hosted
      weights of the display face, which is a choice we made with our eyes open
      and which the number above will keep reminding us about.
    </p>
  </section>

{% endcall %}
